# 8. Proposed revised Section 5

**Status: Draft for attorney review — not certified legally compliant.**

This version includes the requested commercial structure and practices substantiated or supported by the research.

It assumes VRYOH will actually provide online cancellation, confirmation emails, and annual renewal notices.

## 5. PRICING, BILLING, AUTOMATIC RENEWAL, CANCELLATION AND REFUNDS

**5.1 Subscription Plans and Pricing**

VRYOH offers subscription services exclusively for business and commercial use.

Subscription pricing is stated in United States dollars and is calculated per business location.

The available plans are:

**Monthly Plan:** $30 per location per month.

**Annual Plan:** $300 per location per year, equivalent to $25 per month, billed annually in advance.

Applicable taxes, if any, will be added to the subscription price.

**5.2 Automatic Renewal**

All subscriptions renew automatically unless canceled before the next scheduled renewal.

Monthly subscriptions automatically renew each month, with recurring billing on the 25th day of the month.

Annual subscriptions automatically renew for successive one-year periods on the anniversary of the original subscription date.

By subscribing, the customer authorizes Solofella LLC to charge the selected payment method according to the subscription plan and applicable renewal schedule.

The applicable price, billing frequency, renewal terms, and cancellation instructions will be disclosed before the customer completes payment.

**5.3 Initial Monthly Billing**

Customers who subscribe to a monthly plan between scheduled billing dates may receive a prorated initial charge covering the period from activation through the day preceding the next billing date.

The initial charge and the date and amount of the next recurring charge will be displayed before payment confirmation.

Subsequent monthly charges will occur on the 25th of each month.

**5.4 Subscription Confirmation**

Following subscription activation, VRYOH will send an electronic confirmation containing the selected plan, applicable charges, billing frequency, renewal terms, and cancellation instructions.

**5.5 Cancellation**

Customers may cancel their subscriptions at any time through the cancellation function available in their VRYOH account.

Cancellation stops future automatic renewals.

Unless otherwise required by applicable law, cancellation does not immediately terminate access to services already paid for. The subscription remains active until the end of the current paid billing period.

Customers must cancel before the next scheduled renewal charge to prevent renewal.

VRYOH will provide electronic confirmation of cancellation.

**5.6 Annual Renewal Reminders**

VRYOH will send an electronic renewal reminder approximately 30 days before a scheduled annual renewal.

The reminder will include the renewal date, applicable subscription price, renewal period, and instructions for cancellation.

Any additional notices required by applicable law will also be provided.

**5.7 Price Changes**

Solofella LLC may change subscription prices by providing customers with advance notice.

VRYOH will ordinarily provide at least 30 days' advance notice of a price increase.

Price changes will apply to a future renewal period and not retroactively to a billing period already paid for.

Where applicable law requires additional notice, affirmative consent, cancellation rights, or refunds, those requirements will govern.

**5.8 Refunds**

Subscription fees are non-refundable except where required by applicable law or expressly agreed to by Solofella LLC.

Cancellation does not ordinarily entitle the customer to a refund or prorated credit for the unused portion of a paid subscription period.

Any refund rights required by applicable law remain unaffected.

